  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suppli are the Roman relative of the arancino: oval rice croquettes described as "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "al telefono",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "al-telefono"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " because of the mozzarella strings that pull out when you break them open. Unlike "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "suppli",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "suppli"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " from Sicily, these use a tomato-braised rice rather than saffron. Makes about 15."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The rice must be completely cold before shaping or the suppli will not hold together in the hot oil. Plan ahead and make the rice mixture at least an hour before frying."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 5,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "short-grain-rice",
              "amount": 350,
