          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 3 tablespoons of olive oil in a medium saucepan. Cook the onion and pancetta over medium heat for 5 minutes. Add the rice and stir for 1 minute. Add the crushed tomatoes and stock. Cook uncovered, stirring occasionally, for 18 to 20 minutes until the rice is tender and the mixture is thick and dry. Remove from heat, stir in the parmesan and egg yolks, and spread onto a tray. Cool completely."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Wet your hands. Take about 60 g of the cold rice mixture and flatten into an oval. Place a cube of mozzarella in the centre and press the rice firmly around it into an oval croquette shape. Repeat with all the mixture."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Set up three bowls: flour, beaten egg, and breadcrumbs. Roll each suppli in flour, then egg, then breadcrumbs, pressing the coating on firmly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 1 litre of oil to 175C in a deep saucepan. Fry in batches of 4 for 3 to 4 minutes, turning, until golden all over. Drain on kitchen paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve immediately while the mozzarella is still molten."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Suppli bursting open in the oil"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The coating was not thick enough or had gaps. Ensure the rice is well sealed around the mozzarella and press the crumb coating on firmly at every stage."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "No telephone string effect"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The mozzarella needs to be fresh and high-moisture. Drain it well before using. Low-moisture block mozzarella will not stretch."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Coating falls off during frying"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The suppli were not chilled before frying or the coating stages were rushed. Chill for 15 minutes before frying and do not skip the flour stage."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suppli are the snack food of Rome. Every pizzeria in the city serves them as an antipasto while you wait for the pizza. They are eaten standing up, burning your fingers. Romans are fiercely proud of suppli versus arancini. They are not the same thing."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
